course: dictionary
lesson: 1206
title: What is Buddhism?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Buddhism is a religion and a way of life. It follows the teaching of the Buddha, a man called Siddhartha Gautama. Buddhism is a name, so it starts with a capital letter.
explain: Look at the clues in «Buddhism was founded by Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha, in India about 2500 years ago.» Founded means started or begun. So Buddhism began with one person, long ago, in India.
explain: The clues in «Buddhism aims to end suffering through wisdom and kindness» tell you what it is for. Aims means its goal is, and suffering means pain or unhappiness. Buddhists try to end suffering by being wise and kind.
explain: To check your idea, swap in your own meaning and read the sentence again. If it still makes sense, you have understood the word.
fact: Buddhism is a religion and way of life that follows the teaching of the Buddha.
fact: The Buddha is Siddhartha Gautama.
fact: «Buddhism» is a proper noun, the name of a religion, so it starts with a capital letter.
fact: Buddhists meditate, which means sitting quietly and focusing the mind.
fact: Buddhism is common in countries such as Thailand, Sri Lanka, Japan and Tibet.
exercise: «Buddhism was founded by Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha, in India about 2500 years ago.» What does founded mean here? | Written in a book | Ended | *Started or begun | Forgotten
exercise: «Buddhism aims to end suffering through wisdom and kindness.» What is the aim of Buddhism? | To win every game | To make people rich | *To end suffering | To build the biggest building in the world
exercise: What is Buddhism? | *A religion and way of life that follows the teaching of the Buddha | A type of paint for walls | A kind of food from Thailand | A large river in Japan
test: In Buddhism, what does the lotus stand for? | A loud sound | *Something pure rising from mud | A type of temple door | Something dirty that stays in the water
test: Who is the Buddha? | Nirvana | Karma | Gautama the King | *Siddhartha Gautama
exam: «Meditation means sitting quietly and focusing the mind, often on the breath.» What does meditation mean? | *Sitting quietly and focusing the mind | Singing loudly with friends | Running fast around a field | Eating a big meal
